{"id": 335, "stem": "<div class=\"relative w-full min-w-0 max-w-full self-stretch\" id=\"question-text\"><span><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><mark class=\"bg-transparent dark:text-neutral-100\" data-markjs=\"true\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">A</mark> 28-year-old woman, gravida 2 para 2, comes to the office with worsening shortness of breath over the past week.\u00a0 She had a recent episode of hemoptysis.\u00a0 The patient has also had ongoing vaginal bleeding after the uncomplicated vaginal delivery of her son 9 weeks ago.\u00a0 She has no bleeding elsewhere and has not resumed sexual intercourse.\u00a0 On physical examination, the uterus is enlarged and the adnexa are normal.\u00a0 Laboratory studies show markedly increased \u03b2-hCG levels.\u00a0 Chest radiograph reveals multiple bilateral lung nodules.\u00a0 Which of the following would most likely be found on endometrial curettage in this patient?\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c</p></span></div>", "options": [{"label": "A", "text": "Bundles of smooth muscle cells with fibrosis"}, {"label": "B", "text": "Diffusely hydropic chorionic villi"}, {"label": "C", "text": "Fetal tissue with triploid karyotype"}, {"label": "D", "text": "Glands lined by atypical columnar epithelial cells"}, {"label": "E", "text": "Proliferation of cytotrophoblasts and syncytiotrophoblasts"}], "correctAnswer": "E", "explanation": "<div class=\"relative w-full min-w-0 max-w-full self-stretch\" id=\"question-explanation\"><span class=\"\"><div id=\"div_T81277\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><div class=\"group/triggerable\" data-is-open=\"false\"><div class=\"group/draggable\" data-is-draggable=\"true\" data-is-dragging=\"false\"><div class=\"group/resizable relative\" data-is-maximized=\"false\" data-is-resizable=\"true\" data-is-resizing=\"false\"><div class=\"relative max-w-full\"><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"pointer-events-none absolute left-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-8 z-10 transition-opacity duration-200 bg-gradient-to-r from-white dark:from-nbme-primary-dark-800 warm:from-egg-sour-50 to-transparent opacity-0\"></div><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"pointer-events-none absolute right-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-8 z-10 transition-opacity duration-200 bg-gradient-to-l from-white dark:from-nbme-primary-dark-800 warm:from-egg-sour-50 to-transparent opacity-0\"></div><div class=\"max-w-full overflow-x-auto [&amp;_td]:min-w-[8rem] [&amp;_th]:min-w-[8rem]\"><table class=\"border bg-transparent dark:text-white border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white hover:bg-transparent warm:hover:bg-transparent dark:hover:bg-transparent cursor-default mt-2 mb-3\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><tbody style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" colspan=\"5\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><mark class=\"bg-transparent dark:text-neutral-50\" data-markjs=\"true\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">H</mark>istology of gestational trophoblastic disease</strong></p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Diagnosis</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Classification</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Trophoblasts</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Villi</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Fetal/embryonic tissue</strong></p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Partial mole</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Benign</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Focally hyperplastic</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Focally enlarged, hydropic</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Present, triploid</p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Complete mole</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Benign</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Diffusely hyperplastic</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Diffusely enlarged, hydropic</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Absent</p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Invasive mole</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Malignant</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Diffusely hyperplastic with myometrial invasion</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Diffusely enlarged, hydropic</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Absent</p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Gestational choriocarcinoma</strong></p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Malignant</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Diffusely anaplastic/necrotic with vascular invasion</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Absent</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Present or absent</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Gestational trophoblastic disease (GTD) is a spectrum of disease characterized by <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">abnormal trophoblast proliferation</strong>.\u00a0 Complete and partial hydatidiform moles (HMs) are more benign, premalignant forms of GTD caused by aberrant fertilization events.\u00a0 In contrast, <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">gestational choriocarcinomas</strong> and invasive moles are <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">malignant</strong> gestational trophoblastic neoplasias.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Gestational choriocarcinomas are most commonly preceded by a molar pregnancy (complete or partial HM) but can develop following any type of pregnancy (eg, term/preterm, ectopic, abortion).\u00a0 Patients typically have abnormal <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">vaginal bleeding</strong>, uterine enlargement, and <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">markedly elevated \u03b2-hCG levels</strong>.\u00a0 Choriocarcinoma is aggressive and rapidly invades the uterine wall with <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">hematogenous</strong> spread thereafter.\u00a0 The <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">lungs</strong> are the most common site of distal metastasis; therefore, presenting symptoms can include shortness of breath and hemoptysis, as in this patient.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Grossly, gestational choriocarcinoma is seen as a bulky intrauterine mass that is usually soft and yellow-white with extensive areas of necrosis and hemorrhage.\u00a0 Histologically, there are <a class=\"hint\" data-exhibit-id=\"exhibit-y1ipeg1gvk0hi1lru12qtus8\" href=\"#exhibit-exhibit-y1ipeg1gvk0hi1lru12qtus8\">abnormal proliferation</a> of anaplastic, mononuclear <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">cytotrophoblasts</strong> and multinuclear <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">syncytiotrophoblasts</strong>.\u00a0 Notably, <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">no chorionic villi are present</strong>.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice A)</strong>\u00a0 <a class=\"hint\" data-exhibit-id=\"exhibit-sllzsny8xcyvaiwou40keig2\" href=\"#exhibit-exhibit-sllzsny8xcyvaiwou40keig2\">Leiomyomas</a> (eg, uterine fibroids) are common benign tumors of the uterine myometrium characterized by bundles of smooth muscle cells with fibrosis.\u00a0 Common symptoms include heavy menstrual bleeding and pelvic pressure/pain.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choices B and C)</strong>\u00a0 Diffusely hydropic villi can be seen in <a class=\"hint\" data-exhibit-id=\"exhibit-bc6kwpr4nomz3twnfss9lq8c\" href=\"#exhibit-exhibit-bc6kwpr4nomz3twnfss9lq8c\">complete HMs</a>, and partial HMs typically contain fetal tissue and focal hydropic villi with a triploid karyotype.\u00a0 Both complete and partial HMs (molar pregnancies) can present with abnormal uterine bleeding and elevated \u03b2-hCG levels; however, they are unlikely in this patient because HMs occur after an aberrant fertilization (ie, with a new pregnancy).\u00a0 This patient has not resumed sexual intercourse since delivery.\u00a0 Invasive moles, which also share diffusely hydropic chorionic villi and may present with lung metastases, can develop only after molar pregnancies; this patient's recent pregnancy was normal.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice D)</strong>\u00a0 The normal endometrium consists of simple columnar epithelial cells.\u00a0 <a class=\"hint\" data-exhibit-id=\"exhibit-hh6i1qv3j47txq3x6xwd2gli\" href=\"#exhibit-exhibit-hh6i1qv3j47txq3x6xwd2gli\">Atypical endometrial hyperplasia</a>, characterized by crowded endometrial glands lined by atypical columnar epithelial cells, can progress to endometrial cancer.\u00a0 It may also cause abnormal uterine bleeding but not usually in postpartum patients.\u00a0 In addition, atypical endometrial hyperplasia is noninvasive and therefore does not present with lung nodules.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Educational objective:</strong>Gestational choriocarcinoma is a malignant form of gestational trophoblastic disease composed of anaplastic cytotrophoblasts and syncytiotrophoblasts without chorionic villi.\u00a0 It often presents as dyspnea/hemoptysis due to pulmonary metastasis from hematogenous spread.\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c</p></span></div>", "educationalObjective": "Gestational choriocarcinoma is a malignant form of gestational trophoblastic disease composed of anaplastic cytotrophoblasts and syncytiotrophoblasts without chorionic villi.  It often presents as dyspnea/hemoptysis due to pulmonary metastasis from hematogenous spread.\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u20